  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a **0-indexed** integer array `nums`. In one operation you can replace any element of the array with **any two** elements that **sum** to it.\n\n* As an example, consider `nums = [5,6,7]`. In one operation, we can replace `nums[1]` with `2` and `4` and convert `nums` to `[5,2,4,7]`.\n\nOutput *the smallest number of operations to make an array that is sorted in **non-decreasing** order*.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [3,9,3]\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: Here are the steps to sort the array in non-decreasing order:\n- From [3,9,3], replace the 9 with 3 and 6 so the array becomes [3,3,6,3]\n- From [3,3,6,3], replace the 6 with 3 and 3 so the array becomes [3,3,3,3,3]\nThere are 2 steps to sort the array in non-decreasing order. Therefore, we return 2.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,2,3,4,5]\nOutput: 0\nExplanation: The array is already in non-decreasing order. Therefore, we return 0.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 105`\n* `1 <= nums[i] <= 109`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
